====================================================================================================
PART 3 — INSIDER: the fee owner pays the 2% token fee to itself
  If the fee address (or anyone it funds) re-rolls, the token fee round-trips to the same owner.
  Its marginal cost per attempt = s_to_third_party + VRF cost only. If the SOL min ALSO goes to the fee
  owner, the insider's marginal cost is VRF cost only.
  Assumes the VRF cost (VRF_COST) is paid out of the SOL minimum s.
  R=   10,000 s=0.003: public cost per 1-of-100,000 =     308.0 SOL | insider if SOL min -> owner:   200.0 SOL | insider if SOL min -> non-owner sink:   300.0 SOL
  R=   10,000 s=0.01: public cost per 1-of-100,000 =   1,008.0 SOL | insider if SOL min -> owner:   200.0 SOL | insider if SOL min -> non-owner sink: 1,000.0 SOL
  R=1,000,000 s=0.003: public cost per 1-of-1,000 =      11.0 SOL | insider if SOL min -> owner:     2.0 SOL | insider if SOL min -> non-owner sink:     3.0 SOL
  R=1,000,000 s=0.01: public cost per 1-of-1,000 =      18.0 SOL | insider if SOL min -> owner:     2.0 SOL | insider if SOL min -> non-owner sink:    10.0 SOL
  [PASS] insider grind cost < 25% of public cost when SOL min goes to the fee owner (R=1M, s=0.003)

====================================================================================================
PART 4 — release + capture as a substitute re-roll (bypass of the re-roll SOL minimum)
  R=   10,000 s=0.003: re-roll 0.00308 SOL vs release+capture 0.00008 SOL -> bypass saves 97%
  R=   10,000 s=0.01: re-roll 0.01008 SOL vs release+capture 0.00008 SOL -> bypass saves 99%
  R=  100,000 s=0.003: re-roll 0.00380 SOL vs release+capture 0.00080 SOL -> bypass saves 79%
  R=  100,000 s=0.01: re-roll 0.01080 SOL vs release+capture 0.00080 SOL -> bypass saves 93%
  R=1,000,000 s=0.003: re-roll 0.01100 SOL vs release+capture 0.00800 SOL -> bypass saves 27%
  R=1,000,000 s=0.01: re-roll 0.01800 SOL vs release+capture 0.00800 SOL -> bypass saves 56%
  [PASS] without a capture SOL minimum >= re-roll SOL minimum, release+capture is cheaper than re-roll

====================================================================================================
PART 5 — rounding: fee = 2% of ratio in base units
  [PASS] every allowed ratio x decimals 0..9: 2% is exact and > 0 (min = 200 tokens at R=10k, d=0)
  Hypothetical ratios outside the allowed set (why ceil + nonzero floor must still be coded):
    ratio_base=     1: floor=   0 ceil=   1
    ratio_base=    25: floor=   0 ceil=   1
    ratio_base=    49: floor=   0 ceil=   1
    ratio_base=    50: floor=   1 ceil=   1
    ratio_base=    99: floor=   1 ceil=   2
    ratio_base= 12345: floor= 246 ceil= 247
  [PASS] floor rounding gives a ZERO fee for ratio_base < 50 (free re-rolls) — ceil gives >= 1
  [PASS] u64 intermediate R_base*bps overflows for R=5M, d=9 only if bps > 3689 (safe at 200, but compute in u128)

====================================================================================================
PART 6 — tokens accrued at the fee address (sell-pressure disclosure)
  fee tokens = 2% * R * (captures + re-rolls). As % of 1B supply for a max-size collection (N*R = 1B):
    full capture +  0 re-rolls per NFT on average -> 2% of total supply sent to the fee address
    full capture +  1 re-rolls per NFT on average -> 4% of total supply sent to the fee address
    full capture +  3 re-rolls per NFT on average -> 8% of total supply sent to the fee address
    full capture + 10 re-rolls per NFT on average -> 22% of total supply sent to the fee address
  Price impact of the fee address selling X tokens into a constant-product pool holding T_lp tokens:
    LP tokens  100M, sell  10M -> spot price -17.4%
    LP tokens  100M, sell  20M -> spot price -30.6%
    LP tokens  100M, sell  60M -> spot price -60.9%
    LP tokens  200M, sell  10M -> spot price -9.3%
    LP tokens  200M, sell  20M -> spot price -17.4%
    LP tokens  200M, sell  60M -> spot price -40.8%
  [PASS] a full capture of a max-size collection alone routes 20,000,000 tokens (2% of supply) to one address

====================================================================================================
PART 7 — SOL minimum vs rent-exempt minimum for the SOL leg
  SOL min 0.000500 SOL: a lamport transfer to an EMPTY system-account fee wallet FAILS (InsufficientFundsForRent) -> re-roll DoS until someone funds it
  SOL min 0.000891 SOL: a lamport transfer to an EMPTY system-account fee wallet succeeds
  SOL min 0.003000 SOL: a lamport transfer to an EMPTY system-account fee wallet succeeds
  [PASS] a SOL minimum below 890,880 lamports can DoS re-rolls if the SOL receiver is emptied

====================================================================================================
SUMMARY: 8/8 checks PASS
